<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 9-mth T-bills 87 pct sold, yield 312 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 9-mth T-bills 87 pct sold, yield 312 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 20 billion levs of nine-month floater coupon T-bills was 86.99 percent sold, yielding 311.63 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry for Monday's auction.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG 3020496025</p>
<p> Auction date		     November 18, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			 November 20, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		    August 20, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    19,999.9 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		47.69 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    17,399.9 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     57.00 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    311.63 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
